# Optional: copy this file to config/gb10.env to change what `sharar-ctl serve 27b|flashnext` uses. Without it
# the defaults below apply (tools/launcher-config.sh); the target's own settings (port, container, drafter) are in
# config/targets/<target>.env and anything set here wins over them. The real file is ignored by Git; do not put
# tokens or credentials here.

# Model cache (Hugging Face layout); missing pinned snapshots are downloaded here on first serve.
# Default: $HF_HOME, else ~/.cache/huggingface.
# SHARAR_HF_CACHE=/path/to/huggingface
# Flash-Next's cache (135 GB), if it lives elsewhere. Default: SHARAR_HF_CACHE.
# SHARAR_FLASHNEXT_CACHE=/path/to/huggingface-flash-next

# Results, traces, drafter runs, parked sessions and logs. Default: ~/.local/share/sharar.
# SHARAR_RESULTS=/path/to/sharar-results

# Runtime image. Default: ghcr.io/abdelfattah-lab/sharar:latest (tools/image.sh), pulled on first serve
# (private while the repository is: docker login ghcr.io first). Set a local tag to serve docker/build.sh's build.
# SHARAR_IMAGE=sharar:qwen38-27b

# Optimized DFlash2/DSpark compute path; requires an image built from current source.
# SHARAR_DRAFT_PRECISION=fp8
# Relaxed speculative acceptance applied to greedy requests that do not set
# accept_top_k/accept_margin: K:M = top-K within M logits (default 2:1.0, measured
# +10% with no detectable quality change); 'off' keeps every request exact.
# SHARAR_ACCEPT_DEFAULT=2:1.0
# The same for sampled requests (1/0), at their own K:M if set (the fast profile:
# on, the 27B at 2:1.0 because its sampled thinking looped at 3:2.0, #11).
# SHARAR_ACCEPT_DEFAULT_SAMPLED=1
# SHARAR_ACCEPT_DEFAULT_SAMPLED_THRESHOLD=2:1.0
# Largest prompt plus output per request (default 262144, the model's native length).
# One request at this length is guaranteed KV pages; batches share the pool.
# SHARAR_MAX_CONTEXT=262144
# Calibrated 3-bit decode copies (the serving profile turns them on: balanced, fast
# and throughput) come from $SHARAR_RESULTS/w3-checkpoints/<target>-current, fetched
# on first serve when the target has a published checkpoint (docs/w3-calibration.md).
# Set a directory to serve another calibration; without one the 27B rounds to
# nearest (about two GSM8K points lower) and Flash-Next serves its FP8 trunk.
# SHARAR_W3_CHECKPOINT=auto

# Optional: record opt-in request traces (token IDs and verification rounds)
# for draft adaptation. Off when unset. Traces are the user's prompts; keep
# them on this machine. The oldest files are pruned above the cap.
# SHARAR_TRACES=/path/to/sharar-traces
# SHARAR_TRACES_MAX_MIB=32768

# Trained drafts. Serving follows $SHARAR_RESULTS/draft-runs/current when a
# checkpoint has been promoted; set SHARAR_DRAFT=pinned to force the publisher
# draft or SHARAR_DRAFT=/dir to serve a specific `sharar train` checkpoint.
# SHARAR_DRAFT=pinned
# SHARAR_DRAFT_RUNS=/path/to/sharar-results/draft-runs
# SHARAR_TRAIN_STOP_GRACE_S=1200     # time allowed for the final held-out evaluation on `train stop`
# SHARAR_TRAIN_LR=1e-4
# SHARAR_TRAIN_HOLDOUT_TOKENS=20000
